WEBVTT

00:00:01.158 --> 00:00:02.283
[PHOENIX]
My name is Phoenix Wright.

00:00:02.366 --> 00:00:04.325
And I'm a defense attorney.

00:00:04.408 --> 00:00:06.450
No matter the odds,
it's my job to stand up

00:00:06.533 --> 00:00:08.866
for those who have no one
else in their corner.

00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:11.741
I'll do whatever it
takes to fight for the truth!

00:00:14.491 --> 00:00:16.491
[VOICE]
The time is 1 AM.

00:00:23.366 --> 00:00:25.241
There goes the
deadline that we were given.

00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:26.866
And the jewel's still
resting safe and sound

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:28.116
under lock and key.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.366
Bet he got scared
'cause he knew

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:32.116
ol' "big" Dick Gumshoe
and his crew was here.

00:00:38.866 --> 00:00:42.491
Aw, for cryin' out loud!
We've been bamboozled!

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:44.241
[MASK laughs]

00:00:44.325 --> 00:00:46.241
[BOTH gasp]

00:00:46.325 --> 00:00:48.116
[MASK]
Sorry to get your hopes up.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:50.075
Those are the breaks.

00:00:50.158 --> 00:00:52.116
Mask DeMasque,
the phantom thief!

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:53.325
We shall meet again, detective.

00:00:53.408 --> 00:00:56.116
When the moon
is bright and full.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:01:00.033
[MASK laughs]

00:02:35.533 --> 00:02:40.075
[PHOENIX hums]

00:02:40.158 --> 00:02:42.741
Are you seriously
cleaning the toilet again?

00:02:42.825 --> 00:02:45.533
No work, so I gotta
make myself useful somehow.

00:02:45.616 --> 00:02:49.658
Oh, wow, that's just pathetic.
Hope I don't end up like you.

00:02:49.741 --> 00:02:51.783
[PHOENIX growls]
You might.

00:02:51.866 --> 00:02:53.408
Especially if you slack off
on your training.

00:02:53.491 --> 00:02:54.741
[MAYA]
Get off my case.

00:02:54.825 --> 00:02:57.283
I'm way too busy working
to train right now.

00:02:57.366 --> 00:02:58.533
[PHOENIX] Busy working
on "becoming one"

00:02:58.616 --> 00:02:59.825
with the couch, right?

00:02:59.908 --> 00:03:02.033
Hey! I know you've been
playing games all night

00:03:02.116 --> 00:03:03.408
when, in reality,

00:03:03.491 --> 00:03:05.158
you should be trying to
gather up some new clients.

00:03:05.241 --> 00:03:08.158
[PEARL] Oh, you two having
one of your couple's spats?

00:03:08.241 --> 00:03:09.325
[BOTH gasp]

00:03:09.408 --> 00:03:11.658
My gosh. You're so cute!

00:03:11.741 --> 00:03:13.200
--[MAYA] Pearls?
--[PHOENIX] Pearl!

00:03:20.658 --> 00:03:21.991
told you about it by now.

00:03:22.075 --> 00:03:23.116
Ah?

00:03:24.283 --> 00:03:26.450
Kurain Village treasures? Huh.

00:03:26.533 --> 00:03:29.158
Yup! Straight from me
and Pearls's hometown!

00:03:29.241 --> 00:03:31.241
The exhibition doesn't
actually get started until

00:03:31.325 --> 00:03:32.950
next week, but the
promoter was nice enough

00:03:33.033 --> 00:03:35.658
to give us some VIP passes
so we could go early.

00:03:35.741 --> 00:03:36.991
VIPs!

00:03:37.075 --> 00:03:39.908
So I decided to go all out
and dress extra fancy.

00:03:39.991 --> 00:03:41.366
Whattaya think?

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:43.450
[PHOENIX] That's, like, the
only thing you ever wear.

00:03:43.533 --> 00:03:45.491
Yep, good 'ol Maya Fey.

00:03:45.575 --> 00:03:47.700
She's the younger sister
of my friend and mentor,

00:03:47.783 --> 00:03:49.783
the late Mia Fey.

00:03:49.866 --> 00:03:52.658
I met her a couple of
years ago, and even defended her

00:03:52.741 --> 00:03:56.408
when she was falsely accused
of Mia's tragic murder.

00:03:56.491 --> 00:03:57.783
They're from Kurain Village,

00:03:57.866 --> 00:04:00.741
home of the mysterious
Spirit Channeling technique.

00:04:00.825 --> 00:04:03.200
Maya's the daughter
of the Kurain School's master

00:04:03.283 --> 00:04:06.033
and is training to become
a spirit medium herself.

00:04:06.116 --> 00:04:07.825
Of course, the
precocious little girl

00:04:07.908 --> 00:04:09.325
is Pearl Fey.

00:04:09.408 --> 00:04:10.533
She's Maya's cousin,

00:04:10.616 --> 00:04:13.533
and also a young spirit
medium in training.

00:04:13.616 --> 00:04:15.783
The promo poster
looks better than I'd hoped!

00:04:15.866 --> 00:04:18.158
They even got a great picture
of the sacred urn!

00:04:18.241 --> 00:04:20.616
[gasps]
I still feel bad.

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:21.825
First, I broke the urn,

00:04:21.908 --> 00:04:23.741
and then I put it back
together all wrong.

00:04:23.825 --> 00:04:25.325
It's fine!

00:04:25.408 --> 00:04:27.366
I'm sure Mystic Ami's just happy
to know that you did the best

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:29.658
that you possibly could!

00:04:29.741 --> 00:04:31.908
[PHOENIX] A year ago,
while we were investigating

00:04:31.991 --> 00:04:35.158
a murder case in Kurain Village,
little Pearl accidentally

00:04:35.241 --> 00:04:38.741
shattered the sacred urn that
contains the spirit of Ami Fey,

00:04:38.825 --> 00:04:41.158
the school's founder
and protector.

00:04:41.241 --> 00:04:42.450
But by breaking the urn,

00:04:42.533 --> 00:04:44.741
she unwittingly broke
the case as well.

00:04:46.741 --> 00:04:47.908
[REPORTER 2A]
In other news,

00:04:47.991 --> 00:04:49.325
police are searching for
clues after a theft from

00:04:49.408 --> 00:04:51.866
the upcoming treasure exhibit
at Lordly Tailor hall.

00:04:51.950 --> 00:04:53.283
[MAYA]
Eh?

00:04:53.366 --> 00:04:56.325
The rare item stolen, an urn,
was taken last night.

00:04:56.408 --> 00:04:57.825
[gasps]

00:04:57.908 --> 00:04:59.366
[REPORTER 2A] Authorities
believe the heist was the work

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:03.075
of the notorious, so-called
"Phantom thief," Mask DeMasque.

00:05:03.158 --> 00:05:04.741
Masque the Mask?

00:05:04.825 --> 00:05:06.241
A criminal mastermind.

00:05:06.325 --> 00:05:08.366
A thief that targets
rare treasures.

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:11.741
He's like a ghost, and
no one knows who he really is!

00:05:11.825 --> 00:05:12.866
Hence the name.

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:15.366
I just can't
believe they stole it.

00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:17.616
That urn is sacred to us.

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:20.200
Oh, no!

00:05:34.450 --> 00:05:35.825
Ahh...

00:05:35.908 --> 00:05:37.450
The bitterness
stimulates the tongue,

00:05:37.533 --> 00:05:39.866
while the richness
warms the throat!

00:05:39.950 --> 00:05:44.033
Exquisite. Life is
about stimulation.

00:05:44.116 --> 00:05:47.241
And not going through all the
highs and lows it can offer.

00:05:47.325 --> 00:05:48.741
Leaves one sour.

00:05:48.825 --> 00:05:51.533
We're on the scene at the
Lordly Tailor exhibit hall...

00:05:51.616 --> 00:05:54.658
Tch. This ought
to be a real party.

00:06:00.575 --> 00:06:05.491
[MAYA growls] Stupid jerk!
I mean, who would steal our urn?

00:06:05.575 --> 00:06:06.575
All right, then.

00:06:06.658 --> 00:06:07.991
Since it's our treasure
that was stolen,

00:06:08.075 --> 00:06:09.408
it's up to you to
find the thief!

00:06:09.491 --> 00:06:11.325
--[gasps]
--Yeah, she's right!

00:06:11.408 --> 00:06:13.825
The only person who
can get it back is you!

00:06:13.908 --> 00:06:16.075
But I'm just a defense
attorney, not a private eye.

00:06:16.158 --> 00:06:18.116
Hey! Don't start making excuses!

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:20.491
A real hero will gladly do
whatever it takes to help out

00:06:20.575 --> 00:06:22.200
his beloved maiden in need!

00:06:22.283 --> 00:06:23.325
[PHOENIX]
Man, I can't win against

00:06:23.408 --> 00:06:25.741
Pearl's fairy tale
ideas about romance.

00:06:25.825 --> 00:06:27.408
But how are we gonna get inside?

00:06:27.491 --> 00:06:29.450
It won't be easy.
[gasps]

00:06:29.533 --> 00:06:31.241
[MAYA]
Excuse me. Coming through.

00:06:31.325 --> 00:06:33.575
Hold it, lady!
No outsiders allowed!

00:06:33.658 --> 00:06:35.408
I am not an outsider, pal!

00:06:35.491 --> 00:06:38.700
I even have my lawyer and
my cousin here with me!

00:06:38.783 --> 00:06:40.491
[PHOENIX] Why would
having a cousin matter?

00:06:40.575 --> 00:06:41.783
[ANDREWS]
Mr. Wright!

00:06:41.866 --> 00:06:44.325
[gasps]
Ms. Andrews!

00:06:45.658 --> 00:06:48.533
[ANDREWS] Thanks again
for your help last time.

00:06:48.616 --> 00:06:50.408
I was just doing my job, ma'am.

00:06:50.491 --> 00:06:53.033
Anyway, I didn't expect
to see you here.

00:06:53.116 --> 00:06:54.700
[PHOENIX]
This is Ms. Adrian Andrews.

00:06:54.783 --> 00:06:57.033
Former talent agent
and a crucial figure in

00:06:57.116 --> 00:06:58.825
the Nickel Samurai case.

00:07:01.158 --> 00:07:02.950
[ANDREWS] Things have changed a
lot for me since the last time

00:07:03.033 --> 00:07:04.408
we saw each other.

00:07:04.491 --> 00:07:07.325
I'm now head of events and
promotion for Lordly Tailor.

00:07:09.616 --> 00:07:11.783
I am truly sorry
about all of this.

00:07:11.866 --> 00:07:13.283
I've failed you.

00:07:13.366 --> 00:07:14.700
[gasps]

00:07:14.783 --> 00:07:17.241
Your precious urn was
stolen from right under my nose.

00:07:17.325 --> 00:07:20.616
I take full responsibility.
But, I promise--

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:23.325
No! The person responsible
is the phantom thief!

00:07:23.408 --> 00:07:24.783
[gasps]

00:07:24.866 --> 00:07:28.033
We know this is the last
thing you wanted to happen.

00:07:28.116 --> 00:07:31.075
Thanks for that. And I'll
try to make things right.

00:07:31.158 --> 00:07:33.241
You can start by telling us
everything you know

00:07:33.325 --> 00:07:34.616
about the crime.

00:07:34.700 --> 00:07:36.700
Well, first off, the phantom
thief himself sent us

00:07:36.783 --> 00:07:39.241
a calling card of
sorts ten days ago.

00:07:39.325 --> 00:07:40.450
[PHOENIX]
What did it say?

00:07:40.533 --> 00:07:41.908
[ANDREWS] That he was
planning on stealing

00:07:41.991 --> 00:07:45.033
the most valuable piece in
the Kurain Village exhibit.

00:07:45.116 --> 00:07:47.283
Guess the urn's more
valuable than it looks, huh?

00:07:47.366 --> 00:07:49.825
That urn has Mystic
Ami's spirit inside of it,

00:07:49.908 --> 00:07:51.658
which makes it
unbelievably valuable!

00:07:51.741 --> 00:07:53.075
Hard to believe.

00:07:53.158 --> 00:07:54.700
We had an appraisal
done that discovered

00:07:54.783 --> 00:07:56.991
it had zero monetary value.

00:07:57.075 --> 00:07:58.408
Zero...?

00:07:58.491 --> 00:08:00.283
But I did my best to
polish it and make it look

00:08:00.366 --> 00:08:01.741
like it was worth millions!

00:08:01.825 --> 00:08:04.533
I think it's quite a beautiful
work of art, honestly!

00:08:04.616 --> 00:08:07.158
Aw... Poor Mystic Ami...

00:08:07.241 --> 00:08:09.450
Oh, but of course
money isn't everything!

00:08:09.533 --> 00:08:12.116
You simply can't put
a price on historical value.

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:14.075
Not to mention on a soul!

00:08:14.158 --> 00:08:16.408
I misspoke! Please forgive me!

00:08:22.741 --> 00:08:24.450
[ANDREWS]
This is where it was stored.

00:08:24.533 --> 00:08:26.116
So it was in here?

00:08:26.200 --> 00:08:28.158
Doesn't really look like
a crime scene to me.

00:08:28.241 --> 00:08:30.825
[GUMSHOE]
Fancy seeing you again.

00:08:30.908 --> 00:08:32.366
[PHOENIX]
Detective Gumshoe!

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:34.658
It's nutty. What are the odds?

00:08:34.741 --> 00:08:37.033
How are you there
every single time?

00:08:37.116 --> 00:08:39.533
Aren't you a homicide detective?

00:08:39.616 --> 00:08:43.366
Look! Over there!
It's Mystic Ami!

00:08:43.450 --> 00:08:46.950
Oh. Very impressive.

00:08:47.033 --> 00:08:49.033
But what is she
doing over there...?

00:08:49.116 --> 00:08:50.533
Something wrong Ms. Andrews?

00:08:50.616 --> 00:08:52.741
[ANDREWS]
Ah? Oh, no.

00:08:52.825 --> 00:08:55.616
But the little girl is right,
that's a statue of Ami Fey,

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:57.116
the founder of the
Kurain School's

00:08:57.200 --> 00:08:58.825
spirit channeling technique.

00:08:58.908 --> 00:09:01.491
It was delivered
yesterday afternoon.

00:09:01.575 --> 00:09:03.200
Just think about it Mystic Maya,

00:09:03.283 --> 00:09:04.866
someday you'll take over
the clan and become

00:09:04.950 --> 00:09:06.741
the master of Kurain.
Isn't it cool?

00:09:06.825 --> 00:09:08.783
Uh. Oh, yeah!

00:09:08.866 --> 00:09:12.075
My, my, might this be
a meeting of the minds?

00:09:12.158 --> 00:09:13.075
[GROUP]
Hmm?

00:09:13.158 --> 00:09:16.158
[LUKE chuckles]

00:09:16.241 --> 00:09:18.033
Wait. Who's this?

00:09:18.116 --> 00:09:20.575
Welcome to my little soiree.

00:09:20.658 --> 00:09:22.533
A Feast of Chaos!

00:09:24.616 --> 00:09:29.866
[LUKE chuckles] I see it as
clearly as the nose on my face.

00:09:29.950 --> 00:09:31.533
You do? But what is it?

00:09:31.616 --> 00:09:33.075
[LUKE]
Zvarri!

00:09:33.158 --> 00:09:36.533
And once again, the truth so
elegantly reveals itself to me.

00:09:36.616 --> 00:09:39.950
I see a lawyer
and a spirit medium.

00:09:40.033 --> 00:09:42.325
Both but beginners in their
particular professions.

00:09:42.408 --> 00:09:44.950
Say what? How could you
know all that just by looking?

00:09:45.033 --> 00:09:46.908
[LUKE] How, you ask?
For a skeptical mind,

00:09:46.991 --> 00:09:49.241
"how" is as pertinent
a question as "why."

00:09:49.325 --> 00:09:52.158
I am a tried and true
traveler of both time and space.

00:09:52.241 --> 00:09:54.491
As well as a man who
drifts through dreams.

00:09:54.575 --> 00:09:57.200
I might call him a lot of
things, but not any of those.

00:09:57.283 --> 00:09:59.158
He's just trying
to put on a show.

00:09:59.241 --> 00:10:03.075
The poster for the exhibition
had a little blurb about you.

00:10:03.158 --> 00:10:04.575
And the attorney's
badge I'm wearing

00:10:04.658 --> 00:10:06.616
is kind of a giveaway.

00:10:06.700 --> 00:10:08.116
I am Luke Atmey!

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:10.575
A man unto whom some
have bestowed the title.

00:10:10.658 --> 00:10:12.158
Ace Detective.

00:10:12.241 --> 00:10:13.450
Sounds familiar.

00:10:13.533 --> 00:10:14.741
I've seen him on the news,

00:10:14.825 --> 00:10:16.950
he was on the "Great People
in Town" segment.

00:10:17.033 --> 00:10:18.241
[PHOENIX]
Is that really even a thing?

00:10:18.325 --> 00:10:19.700
Seems there's
a plethora of things

00:10:19.783 --> 00:10:22.533
you don't know, counselor!
It's quite strange.

00:10:22.616 --> 00:10:24.950
Usually, the tales of my
investigative prowess

00:10:25.033 --> 00:10:26.825
precede me wherever I go!

00:10:26.908 --> 00:10:28.241
Very well.

00:10:28.325 --> 00:10:29.908
Please, allow me the pleasure
of enlightening you on

00:10:29.991 --> 00:10:31.950
the topic of myself!

00:10:32.033 --> 00:10:33.908
If this has not permeated
the particular rock

00:10:33.991 --> 00:10:36.116
you're living under,
there is a yin and yang

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:39.325
of good and evil in this city!
I am on the side of light,

00:10:39.408 --> 00:10:41.991
while Mask DeMasque
dwells in darkness!

00:10:42.075 --> 00:10:44.866
And when his shadow
enshrouds all under its pall,

00:10:44.950 --> 00:10:47.408
I shall turn a spotlight on
that ghostly figure

00:10:47.491 --> 00:10:49.575
and expose him to the world!

00:10:49.658 --> 00:10:51.825
You get the feeling his
voice is his favorite sound?

00:10:51.908 --> 00:10:53.408
[PHOENIX]
Mm-hmm.

00:10:53.491 --> 00:10:55.283
[LUKE] I have been personally
pursuing the pseudonymed phantom

00:10:55.366 --> 00:10:57.991
since the inception of his
immorality, and thwarted

00:10:58.075 --> 00:11:01.075
his latest loathsome larceny
armed only with my intellect

00:11:01.158 --> 00:11:03.825
and insatiable
inquisitive ingenuity!

00:11:03.908 --> 00:11:06.366
One could argue that
we're two sides of the same coin

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:09.991
buying our way into history.
A rivalry for the ages!

00:11:10.075 --> 00:11:12.908
And last night at 1 AM,
we stood face to face

00:11:12.991 --> 00:11:16.283
in the bowels of this building,
engaged in brilliant battle!

00:11:16.366 --> 00:11:18.575
[PHOENIX]
So it was 1 AM. Wait.

00:11:18.658 --> 00:11:20.366
You mean to tell us that you
were on the premises

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:21.991
when the robbery took place?

00:11:22.075 --> 00:11:23.991
But of course. You see...

00:11:24.075 --> 00:11:26.450
Wherever DeMasque dares
to tread, be assured Atmey

00:11:26.533 --> 00:11:28.116
has already set an elegant trap.

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:30.575
Ah. But the trap was
not elegant enough.

00:11:30.658 --> 00:11:33.700
Actually, I allowed him
to escape filled with fantasy.

00:11:33.783 --> 00:11:35.075
An illusion of victory.

00:11:35.158 --> 00:11:37.866
But still, you were
on guard last night. Why?

00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:41.450
The gentlewoman solicited
my services as sentry.

00:11:41.533 --> 00:11:44.325
Twenty days ago, in fact,
which was ten full days,

00:11:44.408 --> 00:11:46.700
before DeMasque declared
his dastardly designs

00:11:46.783 --> 00:11:48.075
to dame Andrews.

00:11:48.158 --> 00:11:50.491
She hired you before the
calling card was delivered?

00:11:50.575 --> 00:11:52.158
I did. I couldn't
shake the feeling

00:11:52.241 --> 00:11:53.741
something bad was
going to happen.

00:11:53.825 --> 00:11:56.200
And her premonition
proved to be prescient.

00:11:56.283 --> 00:11:58.116
The calling card
arrived soon after.

00:11:58.200 --> 00:11:59.241
Indeed!

00:11:59.325 --> 00:12:00.908
And since I am an Ace Detective,

00:12:00.991 --> 00:12:04.033
I expertly arranged an elegant
trap to ensnare the thief.

00:12:04.116 --> 00:12:05.616
If you knew something
was gonna happen,

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:07.491
why not go to the
police for help?

00:12:07.575 --> 00:12:10.575
Feh. Like I need backup from
that bumbling bunch of boobs.

00:12:10.658 --> 00:12:12.825
Why, you-- What did you say?

00:12:12.908 --> 00:12:14.075
Well, previously...

00:12:14.158 --> 00:12:16.075
...I personally pried
a priceless possession

00:12:16.158 --> 00:12:17.658
from the prowling purloiner.

00:12:17.741 --> 00:12:19.658
The masked marauder's
mischief making is matched

00:12:19.741 --> 00:12:21.741
only by my meticulous mind.

00:12:21.825 --> 00:12:23.700
Meanwhile, you metropolitan
meatheads missed

00:12:23.783 --> 00:12:26.616
the mark on Mask
DeMasque's malfeasance.

00:12:26.700 --> 00:12:28.616
[GUMSHOE growls]

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:29.908
So, counselor.

00:12:29.991 --> 00:12:31.825
Am I correct in my
characterization that

00:12:31.908 --> 00:12:34.450
you're committed to
capturing this caped criminal?

00:12:34.533 --> 00:12:35.783
Oh, we'll get 'im!

00:12:35.866 --> 00:12:37.575
I won't let this phantom
clown get away with taking

00:12:37.658 --> 00:12:38.825
Mystic Ami's urn!

00:12:38.908 --> 00:12:40.200
[LUKE]
Positively perfect.

00:12:40.283 --> 00:12:42.033
Please proceed with
perusing the perimeter

00:12:42.116 --> 00:12:43.991
whist I explore elsewhere.

00:12:44.075 --> 00:12:45.700
We shall catch up counselor.

00:12:45.783 --> 00:12:47.200
Happiest of hunting.

00:12:47.283 --> 00:12:48.616
[PHOENIX gruntz]

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:50.491
That tool's a ton to take.

00:12:50.575 --> 00:12:53.075
He'd better start
respecting my authority.

00:12:53.158 --> 00:12:56.116
[phone rings]

00:12:56.200 --> 00:12:57.450
Yeah?

00:12:57.533 --> 00:12:59.033
[MAYA]
Hmm?

00:12:59.116 --> 00:13:02.616
[GUMSHOE] What? Mask DeMasque
really just turned himself in?

00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:03.908
[BOTH gasp]

00:13:07.408 --> 00:13:08.991
[GUMSHOE]
Sit tight, folks.

00:13:09.075 --> 00:13:11.991
The guards are gonna be bringing
him over in just a second.

00:13:12.075 --> 00:13:14.116
I don't think that I've
ever seen you this happy.

00:13:14.200 --> 00:13:15.491
It's a great day!

00:13:15.575 --> 00:13:17.283
We got our criminal
and that weird detective

00:13:17.366 --> 00:13:19.325
can go suck an egg!

00:13:19.408 --> 00:13:22.325
I'm gonna go start typing
up the report, see ya!

00:13:22.408 --> 00:13:23.908
Let's keep up
this winning streak!

00:13:23.991 --> 00:13:27.116
Since he surrendered himself,
does it really count as a win?

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:28.991
Duh! Of course it's a win!

00:13:29.075 --> 00:13:30.741
Why are you so worked up, Maya?

00:13:30.825 --> 00:13:32.616
It should be completely
obvious why,

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:34.033
because we're the victims!

00:13:34.116 --> 00:13:36.116
--Yeah, I guess so.
-[RON] Hey, there.

00:13:36.200 --> 00:13:37.825
Since we're always
doing murder cases,

00:13:37.908 --> 00:13:39.866
I usually think of the victims
as dead people and

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:41.533
that's super upsetting to me!

00:13:41.616 --> 00:13:42.950
[RON]
Excuse me.

00:13:43.033 --> 00:13:45.200
Wait, we gotta get the urn
back for Poor Mystic Ami!

00:13:45.283 --> 00:13:48.450
In case you haven't noticed,
I'm talkin' over here!

00:13:48.533 --> 00:13:49.908
Oh, sorry about that!

00:13:49.991 --> 00:13:51.158
Someone's there?

00:13:51.241 --> 00:13:52.491
Is that the guy?

00:13:52.575 --> 00:13:55.116
Excuse me. But my
name is Ron DeLite.

00:13:55.200 --> 00:13:57.825
And, uh... I'm also
known as Mask DeMasque.

00:13:57.908 --> 00:13:59.200
Or The Phantom Thief.

00:13:59.283 --> 00:14:01.491
Really? You're a
criminal mastermind?

00:14:01.575 --> 00:14:03.783
Oh, yeah! That's right!

00:14:03.866 --> 00:14:05.575
Or is it?

00:14:05.658 --> 00:14:08.200
I guess I can't really say
which one's a character

00:14:08.283 --> 00:14:09.408
and which one's me.

00:14:09.491 --> 00:14:11.700
He doesn't strike me
as the mysterious type.

00:14:11.783 --> 00:14:14.575
I mean... He talks like
he's trying to keep a secret.

00:14:14.658 --> 00:14:15.908
I know those looks.

00:14:15.991 --> 00:14:18.700
The last thing that I want
from you people is pity!

00:14:18.783 --> 00:14:20.575
Okay, sure, we get it!

00:14:20.658 --> 00:14:23.366
Hey! We need you give
us back that urn right now!

00:14:23.450 --> 00:14:26.241
Yeah! I promise
I'll give it to you.

00:14:26.325 --> 00:14:29.366
But can I? Not good
to make promises I can't keep.

00:14:29.450 --> 00:14:31.616
Yo! Speak up when
you're talkin' to me!

00:14:31.700 --> 00:14:32.908
I'm sorry about that!

00:14:32.991 --> 00:14:36.325
But I hate it when people yell!!

00:14:36.408 --> 00:14:37.450
[GROUP]
Ah...

00:14:37.533 --> 00:14:42.741
[pants]
Look, uh. I, uh, kind of.

00:14:42.825 --> 00:14:44.908
I lost the Kurain urn, okay?

00:14:44.991 --> 00:14:45.908
Huh?

00:14:45.991 --> 00:14:49.325
You... What?

00:14:49.408 --> 00:14:51.116
You have gotta be kidding me!

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:53.450
No I, I wish this was
some kind of joke.

00:14:53.533 --> 00:14:55.325
But these things
happen all the time.

00:14:55.408 --> 00:14:57.325
You know, like leaving
your bag on a train.

00:14:57.408 --> 00:14:59.325
You left Mystic Ami's
urn on a train?

00:14:59.408 --> 00:15:00.783
And you were just
casually riding around

00:15:00.866 --> 00:15:02.116
in that getup?

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:04.700
Now calm down! It's just
a hypothetical situation.

00:15:04.783 --> 00:15:06.075
Anyway...

00:15:06.158 --> 00:15:08.658
I'm so sorry!

00:15:08.741 --> 00:15:10.200
This guy.

00:15:10.283 --> 00:15:11.200
[DESIRÉE]
Ronnie!

00:15:11.283 --> 00:15:12.200
[GROUP gasps]

00:15:12.283 --> 00:15:13.700
[RON]
Oh, Dessie!

00:15:13.783 --> 00:15:15.283
Don't worry.

00:15:15.366 --> 00:15:17.491
I'm gonna do everything in my
power to get you outta there.

00:15:17.575 --> 00:15:18.783
I know you will Dessie.

00:15:18.866 --> 00:15:21.325
So, uh...

00:15:21.408 --> 00:15:24.450
Please forgive me,
my name is Desirée DeLite.

00:15:24.533 --> 00:15:26.825
Desirée's my... My lovely wife.

00:15:26.908 --> 00:15:29.783
[gasps]
The phantom thief has a wife?

00:15:29.866 --> 00:15:32.283
My name is Phoenix Wright,
I'm a defense attorney.

00:15:32.366 --> 00:15:33.825
You don't say?

00:15:33.908 --> 00:15:35.658
Then, are you meeting with my
Ronnie because you're gonna

00:15:35.741 --> 00:15:36.825
take on his defense?

00:15:36.908 --> 00:15:38.866
Well, I haven't made up my mind.

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:40.075
Listen up, lady.

00:15:40.158 --> 00:15:42.366
We're the real victims
here, you got that?

00:15:42.450 --> 00:15:44.866
[gasps]
Wait a minute, are you Maya?

00:15:44.950 --> 00:15:45.950
[MAYA]
Huh?

00:15:46.033 --> 00:15:47.741
Do you two know each other?

00:15:47.825 --> 00:15:49.575
She's on the poster. So.

00:15:49.658 --> 00:15:51.700
You're the Kurain
master's daughter, right?

00:15:51.783 --> 00:15:54.533
I didn't realize I was
starting to get so famous.

00:15:54.616 --> 00:15:56.908
Gosh, you're making me blush!

00:15:56.991 --> 00:15:59.283
[PHOENIX]
I thought you were a victim.

00:15:59.366 --> 00:16:02.491
[DESIRÉE] Ronnie did what?
No, I refuse to believe it!

00:16:02.575 --> 00:16:04.241
Why on Earth would
he steal an urn?

00:16:04.325 --> 00:16:05.783
That's a tough question.

00:16:05.866 --> 00:16:08.741
But let me ask you something.
You know, don't you?

00:16:08.825 --> 00:16:10.575
About your husband
and Mask DeMasque?

00:16:10.658 --> 00:16:13.075
That's no secret.
He's pretty open about it.

00:16:13.158 --> 00:16:15.783
I mean, he's practically
DeMasque's biggest fan.

00:16:15.866 --> 00:16:16.991
He's a fan?

00:16:17.075 --> 00:16:19.533
Oh, definitely.
And he can get carried away.

00:16:19.616 --> 00:16:21.408
Wait, would you
clarify that, please?

00:16:21.491 --> 00:16:23.075
What do you mean
by "carried away"?

00:16:23.158 --> 00:16:24.825
He pretends he's
the phantom thief,

00:16:24.908 --> 00:16:26.783
and sometimes,
it's like he believes it.

00:16:26.866 --> 00:16:28.616
It's kooky, but so adorable.

00:16:28.700 --> 00:16:29.783
[PHOENIX]
Ah...

00:16:29.866 --> 00:16:32.158
Ronnie's timid. Always has been.

00:16:32.241 --> 00:16:34.575
So. DeMasque is like his hero.

00:16:34.658 --> 00:16:37.908
His hero? But the
phantom thief is a bad guy!

00:16:37.991 --> 00:16:39.408
[DESIRÉE chuckles]
Anyway.

00:16:39.491 --> 00:16:41.866
If Ronnie had stolen the urn,
wouldn't he still have it?

00:16:41.950 --> 00:16:42.908
I'd think so.

00:16:42.991 --> 00:16:45.408
Well. Yeah.
That would make sense.

00:16:45.491 --> 00:16:46.700
He is odd.

00:16:46.783 --> 00:16:48.866
But I would never let him
do anything illegal.

00:16:48.950 --> 00:16:51.325
Good to know.
I wouldn't think otherwise.

00:16:51.408 --> 00:16:53.200
I believe somebody
must've framed him

00:16:53.283 --> 00:16:54.408
for the robbery.

00:16:54.491 --> 00:16:55.783
Really?

00:16:55.866 --> 00:16:57.991
I realize it's
a lot to ask of you.

00:16:58.075 --> 00:17:00.783
But would you agree
to defend my husband?

00:17:00.866 --> 00:17:02.533
--Well.
--There's a lot more

00:17:02.616 --> 00:17:05.700
to this case than meets the eye,
I know it! Please!

00:17:05.783 --> 00:17:08.075
I'm begging you!

00:17:08.158 --> 00:17:11.033
Mrs. DeLite.

00:17:11.116 --> 00:17:12.366
How's this sound?

00:17:12.450 --> 00:17:14.575
I'll consider it and start
a full investigation.

00:17:14.658 --> 00:17:15.575
Huh?

00:17:15.658 --> 00:17:17.283
Seriously? Thank you.

00:17:17.366 --> 00:17:19.491
I truly appreciate your help!

00:17:19.575 --> 00:17:20.741
How could you...?

00:17:20.825 --> 00:17:23.491
[PEARL gasps, growls]

00:17:23.575 --> 00:17:26.366
I am very disappointed
in you, Mr. Nick!

00:17:26.450 --> 00:17:27.616
What did I do now?

00:17:27.700 --> 00:17:30.200
Don't play dumb!
You're gonna defend that thief!

00:17:30.283 --> 00:17:32.491
He stole our family's
legacy from us!

00:17:32.575 --> 00:17:34.783
But what if it turns out
that Ron DeLite isn't really

00:17:34.866 --> 00:17:36.075
Mask DeMasque after all?

00:17:36.158 --> 00:17:38.075
Oh, because his wife
said he was delusional?

00:17:38.158 --> 00:17:39.908
She was probably lying to us!

00:17:39.991 --> 00:17:42.033
Or she could
be telling us the truth.

00:17:42.116 --> 00:17:43.491
[gasps]

00:17:43.575 --> 00:17:45.033
[PEARL] I can't believe
you'd really defend that jerk

00:17:45.116 --> 00:17:48.950
after what he did to Mystic Ami.
It breaks my heart...

00:17:49.033 --> 00:17:50.991
I can never forgive you!

00:17:51.075 --> 00:17:52.116
[gasps]

00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:53.741
Hang on, Pearls!

00:17:57.116 --> 00:17:58.450
[MAYA whimpers]

00:18:04.325 --> 00:18:06.700
[PEARL]
Mystic Maya. I'm sorry.

00:18:06.783 --> 00:18:08.533
[MAYA]
Eh?

00:18:08.616 --> 00:18:11.075
You and Mr. Nick are
fighting because of me.

00:18:11.158 --> 00:18:14.075
[MAYA] Mm-mm. You didn't do
anything wrong, sweetie.

00:18:14.158 --> 00:18:16.283
But what if it turns out
that Ron DeLite isn't really

00:18:16.366 --> 00:18:18.033
Mask DeMasque after all?

00:18:18.116 --> 00:18:19.616
[MAYA sighs]

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:21.741
So, what do you think
we should do now?

00:18:23.658 --> 00:18:26.366
Talk to her. We'll get
the whole story from Desirée.

00:18:26.450 --> 00:18:27.908
Ah.

00:18:27.991 --> 00:18:31.158
I want to know more about Ron.
Does that sound good to you?

00:18:31.241 --> 00:18:33.075
[gasps]
Yeah.

00:18:37.991 --> 00:18:39.491
[PHOENIX]
Uh, hello?

00:18:39.575 --> 00:18:41.950
Hello? Is anybody here?

00:18:42.033 --> 00:18:43.741
[sighs]
Don't know where he is,

00:18:43.825 --> 00:18:45.533
but that guy is out to lunch.

00:18:45.616 --> 00:18:47.866
I was hoping to get more
info on Mask DeMasque.

00:18:47.950 --> 00:18:49.658
but I guess it'll have to wait.

00:18:54.325 --> 00:18:56.741
[MASK laughs]

00:18:56.825 --> 00:18:58.575
Sorry to get your hopes up.

00:18:58.658 --> 00:19:00.241
Those are the breaks.

00:19:00.325 --> 00:19:02.616
So then. To what do
I owe this pleasure?

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:05.491
Well, first off, sorry for
dropping in unannounced.

00:19:05.575 --> 00:19:07.783
It's cool. Without Ronnie here,

00:19:07.866 --> 00:19:10.533
my only company is all
these costumes and toys.

00:19:10.616 --> 00:19:12.033
There are a lot.

00:19:12.116 --> 00:19:13.783
It's wild.

00:19:13.866 --> 00:19:16.366
To say he's got an
obsession is an understatement.

00:19:16.450 --> 00:19:18.491
I don't know what to
do with him sometimes.

00:19:18.575 --> 00:19:20.408
Anyway. What do you two need?

00:19:20.491 --> 00:19:22.033
Well. I, uh...

00:19:22.116 --> 00:19:23.908
[tea kettle whistles]

00:19:23.991 --> 00:19:25.075
Hold on a second.

00:19:25.158 --> 00:19:26.408
I'll go pour us some tea.

00:19:26.491 --> 00:19:27.533
A-Ah...

00:19:30.616 --> 00:19:32.366
[PHOENIX]
I wanna see what's in there.

00:19:32.450 --> 00:19:34.658
No, that sounds like
something Maya would do.

00:19:34.741 --> 00:19:36.825
I can almost picture
her egging me on.

00:19:36.908 --> 00:19:38.450
Just open it up Nick!

00:19:38.533 --> 00:19:39.991
A little peek won't kill ya.

00:19:40.075 --> 00:19:42.658
[PHOENIX] No, that's not how
an attorney conducts himself!

00:19:42.741 --> 00:19:44.158
Don't be such a scaredy-cat!

00:19:44.241 --> 00:19:45.741
Now's your only chance!

00:19:45.825 --> 00:19:46.908
[PHOENIX groans]

00:19:52.241 --> 00:19:56.075
Yeah. Fine. Just a peek, then.

00:19:56.158 --> 00:19:57.533
All right, little Pearls.

00:19:57.616 --> 00:19:59.158
Time to get to sleuthin'!

00:19:59.241 --> 00:20:00.908
Yeah, okay.

00:20:00.991 --> 00:20:02.283
With all this crazy stuff here,

00:20:02.366 --> 00:20:05.116
this has gotta be the
phantom thief's hideout.

00:20:06.491 --> 00:20:07.741
[gasps, screams]

00:20:07.825 --> 00:20:09.241
[gasps]

00:20:10.366 --> 00:20:12.908
Oh, Mystic Maya, are you okay?

00:20:15.033 --> 00:20:16.325
Ah?

00:20:20.033 --> 00:20:22.075
--[doorbell rings]
--[DESIRÉE] Coming!

00:20:22.158 --> 00:20:23.241
[MAYA gasps]

00:20:23.325 --> 00:20:25.950
Thank you so much.
I really appreciate it.

00:20:26.033 --> 00:20:27.783
[gasps]
Why's he here?

00:20:31.908 --> 00:20:35.241
[PHOENIX] What is this?
Something smooth and hard.

00:20:35.325 --> 00:20:36.658
[gasps]

00:20:36.741 --> 00:20:38.741
Ahoy! Is anyone here?

00:20:38.825 --> 00:20:40.825
Counselor, this
is quite concerning.

00:20:40.908 --> 00:20:42.616
I'm flabbergasted to
find a friend of the law

00:20:42.700 --> 00:20:44.200
flagrantly ignoring it.

00:20:44.283 --> 00:20:46.700
Uh. I'm sorry about that.

00:20:46.783 --> 00:20:50.116
Right. I suppose your
shortage of scruples will be

00:20:50.200 --> 00:20:51.991
of service as you
stand on the side of that

00:20:52.075 --> 00:20:54.700
sinister scofflaw,
some call DeMasque.

00:20:54.783 --> 00:20:56.241
[PHOENIX]
Where did you hear that?

00:20:56.325 --> 00:20:58.283
I'll be there at the trial.

00:20:58.366 --> 00:21:01.033
Providing my perceptions
to the prosecution.

00:21:01.116 --> 00:21:03.116
--[gasps]
--And Zvarri...

00:21:03.200 --> 00:21:06.200
This testimony will
take its toll on you.

00:21:06.283 --> 00:21:09.325
You miserable minion
of Mask DeMasque.

00:21:09.408 --> 00:21:11.075
[sighs]
Minion, eh?

00:21:11.158 --> 00:21:15.908
[LUKE chuckles] Although, I
alone am not your adversary.

00:21:15.991 --> 00:21:18.366
Tomorrow's trial will
introduce a terrible threat

00:21:18.450 --> 00:21:20.991
who will truly thwart
your thriving trajectory.

00:21:21.075 --> 00:21:22.491
What do you mean?

00:21:22.575 --> 00:21:24.533
[LUKE] A defense's most
fearsome foe is a properly

00:21:24.616 --> 00:21:26.908
prepared prosecutor.

00:21:26.991 --> 00:21:28.783
You may be used to
Edgeworth's excellence,

00:21:28.866 --> 00:21:31.241
but your next enemy
is without equal.

00:21:31.325 --> 00:21:33.241
He is correctly called the
most cunning counselor

00:21:33.325 --> 00:21:36.450
in the country.
But you may know him as...

00:21:36.533 --> 00:21:37.991
...Godot!

00:21:38.075 --> 00:21:42.658
[GODOT] Hmph. We're to do battle
in this gladiator's arena.

00:21:42.741 --> 00:21:43.825
[PHOENIX gasps]

00:21:43.908 --> 00:21:45.158
The sole reason

00:21:45.241 --> 00:21:47.825
I've returned from
the ghastly depths of Hell.
